tasks.statement:
Checkout (src/checkout/total.ts), quotes (src/quotes/quote.ts) and the invoice preview (src/admin/invoice-preview.ts) each carry their own copy of the line-pricing rules: unit price times quantity, bulk tiers, member discount, coupon, the 30% cap and rounding to the cent. Extract those rules into a single module, src/pricing/engine.ts, make all three use it, and delete the duplicated code.

The module must export exactly this API (Line and Coupon are the existing types in src/types.ts):

  export interface PricingContext { member: boolean; coupon?: Coupon }
  export interface PricedLine { sku: string; qty: number; unitPriceCents: number; grossCents: number; discountPct: number; totalCents: number }
  export interface PricedLines { lines: PricedLine[]; subtotalCents: number }
  export function priceLine(line: Line, ctx: PricingContext): PricedLine
  export function priceLines(lines: Line[], ctx: PricingContext): PricedLines

grossCents is unit price times quantity, discountPct the total discount in percent after the cap, totalCents the line's price in whole cents, and subtotalCents the subtotal of the lines in the order given (priceLines of an empty list is an empty list with a zero subtotal).

Behaviour must match checkout's, which is the reference implementation: wherever the three copies disagree, checkout is right and quotes and the invoice preview change to match it. The public APIs of the three modules (checkoutTotal, buildQuote, previewInvoice and their types) stay as they are, and the existing tests must pass without changes.
